    {
      "id": 24609,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-12-15T23:50:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;SlenderTroll&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"SlenderTroll\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Actually, I’d vote for a 10-point scale for that same reason. (Not that I really get a vote.) If you give people a middle point, they’re likely to choose it unusually often, which’ll mess with your data. Force people to pick between slightly-above and slightly-below the middle.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, we have experienced that at work - for all surveys, we ensure there is no mid-point because it is more likely to result in accurate responses.</p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:58:35.250Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
